userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: The area of any oblique triangle equals one-half the base times the perpendicular height from the opposite vertex, and that height is the leg of a right triangle giving h = c·sin of the angle adjacent to the perpendicular — whether the foot lands on the base (acute) or on its extension (obtuse).
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): Whether the perpendicular from the apex lands on the base or on its extension, the height is h = c·sin of the angle adjacent to that perpendicular, so Area = ½·b·c·sin α holds for acute and obtuse triangles alike.
DEMO STEPS: 4 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

FULL BLUEPRINT:
{
  "concept": "The area of any oblique triangle equals one-half the base times the perpendicular height from the opposite vertex, and that height is the leg of a right triangle giving h = c·sin of the angle adjacent to the perpendicular — whether the foot lands on the base (acute) or on its extension (obtuse).",
  "figureType": "diagram",
